1. State file -> 
                It is a file which compare desired state and current state.

                If a state file is manauly deleted --> Then we apply --> terraform apply 
                    --> New instance will be created --> because the state which is stored 
                        is delete

                If we manauly stoped the instance --> then terraform will not able to start
                --> Because there is no api provided to start the instance

                If manually change the configuration of instance and --> the configuration is 
                not present in the main.tf file then --> the changes are applicable in the instance 